# The Floor. Act 1, Low Night. District file floor.lwd: the harbour floor at low water.
# Places: floor, gully, drowned, fish. Beats (design/ACT1-PLAN.md section 6): 13 down to the floor,
# 14 the fish, 15 the drowned lamp. Writing helper, 2026-10-16. Private.
# Gates: the floor while tide < -0.27 (the lowest steps flood 23:48); the gully while tide < -0.35
# (shuts 23:42); the drowned lamp's base is covered 23:52. Fog 23:20, rain 23:35 (wind to the SW).
# Merrow at the drowned lamp to 23:40, in the gully 23:40 to 23:45; Lugg at the gully to 23:40;
# Cockle and Dilly at the fish to 23:48. The low light itself is never explained.

# ---- new ids
@fact floor.page_gap
@fact floor.lugg_saw
about: Ferris Lugg, holding Merrow's rope at the gully when the ferry turned, saw a light in the hole of the Old Light, small and low and steady. Merrow says his lantern was out.
by: testimony, whispered

@fact floor.watch_true
about: Merrow's watch, set every Low Night by the harbour office clock, agrees with the Almanac to the minute. His times are good times.
by: the Almanac

@fact floor.dilly_book
about: Dilly Rudd's slate: every child on the floor has bet that the fish dies, and Dilly has taken every bet. If it dies she is ruined. A book that touches the horse is not a book, so she cannot turn it herself.
by: THE CHIT, or Dilly

@fact floor.walk_timed
about: By his prints and the Almanac's gates, the man in size elevens reached the Old Light by about eighteen past ten and had not come back: he was there when the ferry turned.
against: merrow 5
by: SUM, the prints and the Almanac

@fact floor.walk_wrong
about: In pencil: by his stride, the man in size elevens could not have reached the Old Light before half past ten.
by: SUM, in pencil

@fact floor.cullet
about: In the pool under the Brine's yard drain: drops of green glass melted round, not broken, and dry on top. Thrown down tonight, after the floor opened.
against: sabine 5
by: the Damp, or CARBON

@fact floor.merrow_trust
@fact floor.met_lugg
@fact floor.prints_back
@fact floor.hat_lost
@fact floor.lantern_lost
@fact floor.cockle_home
@fact floor.lantern_two
@fact floor.fish_contested
@fact floor.with_merrow
@fact floor.salv.bottle
@fact floor.salv.cork
@fact floor.salv.tin
@fact floor.salv.wire
@fact floor.salv.brass
@fact floor.salv.crown
@fact floor.salv.wick
@fact floor.dilly_covered
@fact floor.merrow_left
@fact floor.copper_taken
@fact floor.gulls_off
@fact floor.move_mudstep
@fact floor.move_hookpull
@fact floor.cockle_guided
@fact floor.bar_told
@fact floor.salv.rope
@fact floor.handline
@fact floor.copper_sunk
@fact floor.cork_short
@fact floor.channel_dug
@fact floor.fight_word
# struck.lugg and down.floor: the Fray's Record entries (SYSTEMS-FULL 18.7, 18.10) for this district.
@fact struck.lugg
@fact down.floor

# Low Night walkers who speak (beat 13).
@char floor.gill
name: Gill
speaker: GILL
about: Agnes Spratt's runner, about twelve. Speaks in Mrs Spratt's words.

@char floor.ruddle_mrs
name: Mrs Ruddle
speaker: MRS RUDDLE
about: Of Tanner's Row. Mother of three in descending sizes.

@char floor.ruddle
name: Mr Ruddle
speaker: MR RUDDLE
about: Of Tanner's Row. Says little, in round numbers.

@var floor.award
default: none
values: none, guild, lowco, congregation, fish
about: Lamb's ruling on the fish (beat 14).

@var floor.bet
default: none
values: none, lives, dies
about: What Lamb staked with Dilly Rudd.

# The fish's fate if nobody turns it and nobody has ruled: the gulls, at the turn of the floor.
@event floor.ev.fish
at: 23:48
when: var.fish == stranded
do: fish = gulls
if: seen(floor.fish.first) => quest(a1.fish, gulls)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the hub
@node floor.hub
place: floor
hub: yes
alt: floor.closed ? tide >= -0.27 | clock >= 23:48
alt: floor.first ? !seen(floor.first)
alt: floor.fog.arrives ? clock >= 23:20 & !seen(floor.fog.arrives)
alt: floor.rain.arrives ? clock >= 23:35 & !seen(floor.rain.arrives)
alt: floor.merrow.returns ? clock >= 23:43 & clock < 23:48 & !seen(floor.merrow.returns) & !has(floor.with_merrow)
nar: The floor at low water: lanterns, the old hull, the fish, and past the gully the drowned lamp with its small light. {when: clock < 23:20}
nar: The floor in fog. The lanterns are rings of light with nobody in them. {when: clock >= 23:20 & clock < 23:35}
nar: Fog and rain. The lanterns are drifting in toward the steps in twos and threes. {when: clock >= 23:35}
nar: Out on the mole Mother is lit. Her beam crosses the floor every half-minute, green, and every walker looks up. {when: mother == burning}
opt: "Walk among the lanterns." -> floor.walkers
opt: "Look at the prints that go out from the foot of the steps." -> floor.prints ? !seen(floor.prints) | (clock >= 23:43 & !has(floor.prints_back)) {verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Go over to the fish and the children walking round it." -> floor.fish.first ? !seen(floor.fish.first) +1
opt: "Go back to the fish." -> floor.fish.again ? seen(floor.fish.first) +1
opt: "Go to the gully, where a very tall man is holding a rope." -> floor.lugg.first ? clock < 23:40 & !has(floor.met_lugg) +2
opt: "Go back to Lugg at the gully." -> floor.lugg.again ? clock < 23:40 & has(floor.met_lugg) +2
opt: "Go to the gully and cross to the drowned lamp." -> floor.gully ? tide < -0.35 +2
opt: "Go to the gully and look across." -> floor.gully.closed ? tide >= -0.35 +2
opt: "Climb about the ribs of the old hull." -> floor.wreck +1 {verb: climb, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Look in the pool under the Brine's drain." -> floor.pool ? tide < -0.31
opt: "Go back up the steps to the quay." -> quay.hub +3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the floor closed
@node floor.closed
place: steps
cost: 1
nar: The lowest steps are under water. The lanterns are all on the steps now, in a line, going up. {when: clock < 23:52}
nar: Out past where the gully was, a lantern still burns in the Old Light, the water climbing to it. Nobody on the steps says who hung it. {when: clock < 23:52 & has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
nar: The floor is closed. Black water over the mud, the hull and the place where the fish was. {when: clock >= 23:52 & clock < 00:20}
nar: The lantern in the Old Light went out at eight minutes to midnight, not all at once. {when: clock >= 23:52 & clock < 00:20 & has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
nar: Somewhere under the water are the prints of the man the town has just been told to hang. The tide is filling them in. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == wreckers}
nar: The floor is quiet. Up at the weigh-house, the Guild is not. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == guild}
nar: Under five feet of water a sack's worth of the Trust's copper is still missing. Tonight the town does not mind. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == trust}
nar: On the steps two women talking about the keeper stop when they see the Shelf's coat. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == keeper}
nar: The sea, named at midnight as the cause, comes in over the floor and does not mind. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == sea}
nar: On the steps a man explains to his son what an insurer is, and gets it wrong in a way the assessor cannot fault. {when: clock >= 00:20 & var.prov == refused}
nar: High water. The sea is at the top step and looking over it. {when: clock >= 05:00}
go: quay.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- arriving
@node floor.first
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: The bottom step, and then the floor of the harbour, which takes the boot to the ankle and holds it a moment.
nar: Grey mud out to the gully. Black pools, each with a lantern standing in it upside down. Past the gully, the stump of the Old Light, leaning, with a small light in a hole in its side.
nar: About sixty of the town are out here in second-best boots, walking the bottom of the sea with the care of guests in a house whose owner has stepped out.
voice: salt: The knees know. Nineteen years since anyone stood this low. The sea is a long way off and it is thinking about you. {dc: 4}
inst: THE ALMANAC: The floor closes from the steps outward at twelve minutes to midnight. The gully goes first, at eighteen minutes to. The Old Light is under by eight minutes to. I give these times once and I do not give them kindly.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.fog.arrives
place: floor
cost: 1
nar: Fog off the bay at twenty past eleven. It takes the far things first, like a creditor: the Spit, the drowned lamp, the hull, then the family nearest, who go on talking from inside it.
nar: A child calls for her father and three fathers answer.
voice: dark: Sound is different now. Nearer, and from the wrong side. {dc: 5}
do: meter(dread, 1)
go: floor.hub

@node floor.rain.arrives
place: floor
cost: 1
nar: Rain at twenty-five to twelve, from the south-west. The walkers begin to drift toward the steps.
inst: THE VANE: South-west! Round she's come, south-west and freshening! Everything said down here now goes up the floor to the town!
do: wet(0.1)
go: floor.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- beat 13: the Low Night walkers
@node floor.walkers
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: Each family keeps its own lantern and its own distance, and each, passing another, says the same four words: "Lowest in nineteen year."
nar: Nearest is a family of five in descending sizes. {when: clock < 23:20}
nar: In the fog they are voices first: a family of five arguing, a boy counting aloud. {when: clock >= 23:20}
opt: "Speak to the family of five." -> floor.walk.family ? !seen(floor.walk.family)
opt: "Ask the boy what he is counting." -> floor.walk.count.fog ? clock >= 23:20 & !seen(floor.walk.count.fog)
opt: "Leave them to the floor." -> floor.hub

@node floor.walk.family
place: floor
cost: 4
nar: The Ruddles of Tanner's Row, and three children who stand in order of height without being asked. Mr Ruddle raises his lantern to the assessor's coat, and then to the assessor.
line: MRS RUDDLE: You're the insurance. Is it wreckers, then? Everyone says.
opt: "It may be." -> floor.walk.family.tell {do: set(said.wreckers); set(said.ruddle_wreckers)}
opt: "I don't know yet. What did you see?" -> floor.walk.family.tell {do: set(said.ruddle_unknown)}
opt: "No. It isn't." -> floor.walk.family.tell {do: set(said.ruddle_no)}
opt: "Thank them and walk on." -> floor.walkers

@node floor.walk.family.tell
place: floor
cost: 3
line: MRS RUDDLE: Twenty to ten, they went. The quay and Mother, all at once, like somebody blowing out a cake.
line: MR RUDDLE: Then back. Ten minutes, near enough. Pink.
line: MRS RUDDLE: Pink as a sore. And Mother never came back with them. She's sulking.
line: MRS RUDDLE: I'll tell Tanner's Row the Shelf says wreckers. {when: has(said.ruddle_wreckers)}
do: set(lamps.pink)
go: floor.walkers

@node floor.walk.count.fog
place: floor
cost: 3
nar: A boy with a jam-jar lantern is counting lanterns, turning slowly, pointing. Forty-one.
nar: He tells the assessor there were forty when the fog came, as a fact between colleagues, and goes off to find his mother.
nar: The assessor counts. Forty-one. Counting the families, one lantern each and two for the Ruddles, the assessor gets forty. The assessor does not count a third time.
voice: dark: You will not find it by looking. Nobody is carrying it. It is just one more. {dc: 6}
voice: dark: A boy miscounted in the fog. That is all. That is the entire matter. {below: 6}
do: meter(dread, 1)
go: floor.walkers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- beat 13: Merrow's prints (C1)
@node floor.prints
alt: floor.prints.back ? clock >= 23:43
alt: floor.prints.soft ? clock >= 23:35
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(prints.read)
nar: Prints go out from the foot of the steps toward the drowned lamp. Size eleven, if the assessor is a judge, which professionally the assessor is.
nar: Going out, the heels are shallow. None come back. Beside them, a second line, very long in the stride.
inst: THE ALMANAC: The floor opened past these steps at eight minutes past ten. The gully at sixteen past.
voice: carbon: He walks out with a weight on the left shoulder. A coil of rope; the right arm swings free. Where the mud firms he lengthens his stride. He knows this floor in the dark. {dc: 6}
check: "[SUM] Pace his stride against yours and time his walk to the gully." -> floor.prints.timed / floor.prints.timed.fail ? !has(floor.walk_timed) & !has(floor.walk_wrong) {skill: sum, dc: 6, verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Leave the prints." -> floor.hub

@node floor.prints.timed
place: floor
cost: 4
do: set(floor.walk_timed)
nar: Six hundred paces to the gully at a stride a hand longer than the assessor's: nine minutes. He went out after eight past ten, waited where the mud is churned, and crossed at sixteen past.
nar: No prints come back. At twenty past ten the man in size elevens was at the Old Light.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.prints.timed.fail
place: floor
cost: 4
do: set(floor.walk_wrong)
nar: By the assessor's sum he reached the gully at half past ten, too late for the ferry. It goes in the Daybook in pencil, wrong by the width of a stride.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.prints.soft
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: The rain has begun on the prints. Each holds a little pocked water, and the edges are going the way of a biscuit left in tea.
check: "[CARBON] Read them before the rain does." -> floor.prints.soft.ok / floor.prints.soft.fail {verb: read, noise: 0, skill: carbon, dc: 5}
opt: "Leave them to the weather." -> floor.hub

@node floor.prints.soft.ok
place: floor
cost: 2
do: set(prints.read)
nar: The assessor reads fast: size eleven, shallow heels going out, a very long stride beside them, and churned mud at the gully's edge where he waited.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.prints.soft.fail
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: One print reads, the next less well, and the third is a small round pond. Somebody walked out. Big boots, probably.
voice: carbon: You are reading water. Wait for whoever made these to come home. Homecoming prints are fresh. {dc: 3}
go: floor.hub

@node floor.prints.back
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(prints.read); set(floor.prints_back)
nar: Over the old dents, fresh, coming in from the gully: size eleven, the heels driven a full inch into the mud, each filling with water.
voice: carbon: He stops here. Shifts the weight to the other shoulder. Goes on. The water in the gully was at his thighs and he did not care for it. {dc: 5}
go: floor.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the old hull, and floor salvage
@node floor.wreck
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: The ribs of an old hull, black with weed. A child going by says it is the Margery Dole, lost with a cargo of tin plate and Methodists.
nar: Thirty-odd gulls sit along the ribs, all facing the fish. {when: clock < 23:48}
nar: Low between the ribs, the corner of a tin box. {when: tide < -0.45 & !has(floor.salv.tin)}
nar: The lowest ribs are under water now. {when: tide >= -0.45 & !has(floor.salv.tin)}
nar: Round the lowest rib, a tarred mooring rope, newer than the wreck by a century. {when: tide < -0.4 & !has(floor.salv.rope)}
nar: Higher up, old cork floats are tangled in the weed. {when: tide < -0.3 & !has(floor.salv.cork)}
opt: "Reach down between the ribs for the tin box." -> floor.salv.tin ? tide < -0.45 & !has(floor.salv.tin) {verb: salvage, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Pick the cork floats out of the weed." -> floor.salv.cork ? tide < -0.3 & !has(floor.salv.cork) {verb: salvage, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Cut the mooring rope free." -> floor.salv.rope ? tide < -0.4 & !has(floor.salv.rope) {verb: salvage, noise: 0.1}
check: "[GRIP] Rig the rope rib to rib toward the gully, a hand line for the way back." -> floor.rig.line.ok / floor.rig.line.fail ? count(i.rope) > 0 & !has(floor.handline) & clock < 23:40 {skill: grip, dc: 5, verb: rig, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Leave the Margery Dole to her gulls." -> floor.hub

@node floor.salv.tin
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(floor.salv.tin); give(s.tin); wet(0.15); meter(cold, 1)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.tin)
nar: The assessor kneels, which the mud receives with interest, and reaches into black water to the elbow. A ship's biscuit tin, good tin, holding the sea and one very old biscuit the assessor does not examine.
go: floor.wreck

@node floor.salv.rope
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(floor.salv.rope); give(i.rope); wet(0.1)
nar: The knot has been in the sea long enough to be a stone. The penknife cuts above it: a coil of good tarred line, and an ache in the wrist.
go: floor.wreck

@node floor.rig.line.ok
place: floor
cost: 6
do: set(floor.handline); take(i.rope)
nar: Rib to rib, a turn and a hitch at each, the last length run to a stake at the gully's lip: a bannister for the sea.
go: floor.wreck

@node floor.rig.line.fail
place: floor
cost: 4
do: take(i.rope); wet(0.2)
nar: The third hitch slips, and the rope goes away down the gully like a snake late for something.
go: floor.wreck

@node floor.salv.cork
place: floor
cost: 2
do: set(floor.salv.cork); give(s.cork)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.cork)
nar: Two cork floats, black with age. They weigh nothing at all, which on this floor tonight is a kind of comfort.
go: floor.wreck

@node floor.pool
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: Under the Brine's yard drain the floor holds a pool: a Hesk ale bottle, and round it green glass the size of teardrops.
opt: "Fish out the bottle." -> floor.salv.bottle ? !has(floor.salv.bottle) {verb: salvage, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Lay the Damp on the glass drops." -> floor.pool.damp ? var.damp_wet != 1 & !has(floor.cullet) {verb: read, noise: 0}
check: "[CARBON] Turn the drops over in the lantern light. The Damp is drowned." -> floor.pool.carbon / floor.pool.carbon.fail ? var.damp_wet == 1 & !has(floor.cullet) {skill: carbon, dc: 7, verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Leave the pool." -> floor.hub

@node floor.pool.damp
place: floor
cost: 2
do: set(floor.cullet)
if: has(soot.east) => set(oven.inferred)
inst: THE DAMP: Wet underneath, from the pool. Dry on top, and crusted. These came down after the water went, which was eight minutes past ten.
nar: The drops are round at the edges, smooth all over.
go: floor.pool

@node floor.pool.carbon
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(floor.cullet)
if: has(soot.east) => set(oven.inferred)
nar: Each drop has round edges, no fracture and a skin on it. On the back of a glove one is dry on its upper face, under salt that has had no tide over it.
voice: carbon: Somebody up there tips a pan down the drain tonight. Hot. {dc: 7}
go: floor.pool

@node floor.pool.carbon.fail
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: Sea glass, the assessor writes. The drop on the glove is not frosted at all. The assessor rubs out sea glass, and has nothing to put in its place.
go: floor.pool

@node floor.salv.bottle
place: floor
cost: 2
do: set(floor.salv.bottle); give(s.bottle_glass); wet(0.05)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.bottle_glass)
voice: undertow: Green glass, in a town where somebody has been very interested lately in green glass. {dc: 7, when: has(prism.green_oven) | has(lens.green)}
go: floor.pool

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ferris Lugg at the gully
@node floor.lugg.first
place: gully
cost: 3
do: set(floor.met_lugg)
nar: At the near edge of the gully a man stands very still, holding a rope that runs across the water to the Old Light. He is the tallest man in Gullet, and holds himself as if apologising for it to a lower ceiling.
nar: He says something. The wind takes it east, to nobody.
inst: THE VANE: West, six metres! He's whispering into it! Every word he owns is going to the Gut! Get to his lee, east of him, his lee side! {when: clock < 23:35}
inst: THE VANE: South-west and wet! His words go north-east, up the floor! Stand north of him or hear nothing! {when: clock >= 23:35}
nar: He looks at the mud on the assessor and holds out a loop of the rope. {when: guise == floor}
opt: "Step round to his lee side, where the wind will bring his words." -> floor.lugg.lee {verb: eavesdrop, noise: 0}
opt: "Ask him to speak up." -> floor.lugg.up
opt: "Leave him holding the rope." -> floor.hub

@node floor.lugg.up
place: gully
cost: 2
nar: Lugg says something else, at the same volume.
voice: hearsay: He said wreckers. You are nearly sure he said wreckers. He might have said weather. Write down wreckers. {below: 6}
opt: "Step round to his lee side." -> floor.lugg.lee {verb: eavesdrop, noise: 0}
opt: "Leave him holding the rope." -> floor.hub

@node floor.lugg.lee
place: gully
cost: 3
nar: On his lee side the words arrive like a letter delivered by a mouse.
line: LUGG: You'll be the Shelf.
line: LUGG: He's over there. In the old lamp. You'll have seen the light.
line: LUGG: Don't tell the Board where he is. Not till the water's back. Will you not?
opt: "I won't tell the Board. Not tonight." -> floor.lugg.promise {do: set(said.lugg_promise); set(heard.lugg.lugg_promise)}
opt: "I can't promise you that." -> floor.lugg.refuse {do: set(said.lugg_refused); set(heard.lugg.lugg_refused)}
opt: "Say nothing. Look at the rope." -> floor.lugg.silent {do: silent_scene = 1}

@node floor.lugg.promise
place: gully
cost: 1
do: rep(lowco, 1)
nar: Lugg nods once, from a great height.
line: LUGG: Then you can cross on it, if you want. It holds Tub. It'll hold the Shelf.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.refuse
place: gully
cost: 1
do: rep(lowco, -1)
nar: Lugg looks back at the rope. The conversation is over on his side, though he remains, very politely, available for any other.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.silent
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The rope hums in the current.
nar: Lugg shifts his grip, and a yard of slack lies within the assessor's reach.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.menu
place: gully
alt: floor.hub ? clock >= 23:40
opt: "What did you see at twenty past ten?" -> floor.lugg.light ? !has(floor.lugg_saw) & !has(said.lugg_refused)
opt: "Why do you whisper?" -> floor.lugg.why ? !seen(floor.lugg.why)
opt: "Cross the gully on his rope." -> floor.gully.rope ? tide < -0.35 & !has(said.lugg_refused) +2 {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Leave him to the rope." -> floor.hub

@node floor.lugg.again
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: Lugg is where he was, a turn of the rope round his wrist and the water higher on his boots. He looks across the gully more often than at anything else.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.light
place: gully
cost: 4
do: set(floor.lugg_saw)
line: LUGG: I was here. Holding. Rope went tight: him climbing in at the hole. Then the light.
line: LUGG: In the hole. Little. Low. Steady. And out on the water the ferry's bell going, and then the big sound, a ship turning, like a cart in a narrow lane.
line: LUGG: Tub says his lantern was out then. Knocked it climbing in.
line: LUGG: I'll not say Tub's a liar. I'll not say I'm blind. You say.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.why
place: gully
cost: 3
line: LUGG: Shouted once. At sea. On the Hesk boat, in fog, before this one. Shouted left.
line: LUGG: Meant the other left.
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Let the silence after that be his, not yours." -> floor.lugg.why.ok / floor.lugg.why.fail {skill: condolence, dc: 6}
opt: "Say you are sorry, and leave it there." -> floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.why.ok
place: gully
cost: 2
do: rep(lowco, 1)
nar: The assessor says nothing. Lugg listens to the water.
line: LUGG: Tub was the one went in after him. Tub doesn't talk about it either. That's why I hold his rope.
go: floor.lugg.menu

@node floor.lugg.why.fail
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The assessor says that it must have been very hard, in the voice the Shelf issues for the purpose. Lugg agrees, in a whisper so courteous it is almost a door closing.
voice: condolence: You said the kind thing. It was the wrong size. {dc: 3}
go: floor.lugg.menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the gully: crossing out
@node floor.gully
place: gully
alt: floor.gully.closed ? tide >= -0.35
cost: 1
nar: The gully is a dozen yards of brown water going inland in a hurry, as if it had heard something. {when: clock < 23:30}
nar: The gully is fuller and faster now, and loud at the edges. {when: clock >= 23:30}
voice: knees: Knee-deep, at a guess. Knees have been asked worse. Not often, and not by the Shelf. {dc: 4}
opt: "Wade straight across." -> floor.gully.wade {verb: wade, noise: 0.3}
check: "[BALLAST] Wade across with the Kit held high, out of the water." -> floor.gully.dry / floor.gully.dunk ? clock < 23:30 {verb: wade, noise: 0.2, skill: ballast, dc: 5}
check: "[BALLAST] Wade across with the Kit held high. It is deeper now." -> floor.gully.dry / floor.gully.dunk ? clock >= 23:30 {verb: wade, noise: 0.2, skill: ballast, dc: 7}
opt: "Cross on Lugg's rope, hand over hand." -> floor.gully.rope ? clock < 23:40 & (seen(floor.lugg.lee) | guise == floor) & !has(said.lugg_refused) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Wade across in Merrow's waders." -> floor.gully.waders ? worn(c.waders) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Wade across leaning on the boathook, a third leg against the current." -> floor.gully.hook ? count(w.boathook) > 0 {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Cross along your hand line." -> floor.gully.rope ? has(floor.handline) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
check: "[SALT] Feel for Nan Cockle's bar where the gulls stand in the water." -> floor.gully.bar / floor.gully.dunk ? has(floor.bar_told) {skill: salt, dc: 6, verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Douse the lantern and cross in the fog, upstream of his light." -> floor.drowned.creep ? clock >= 23:20 & clock < 23:38 & !has(met.merrow) {verb: hide, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Not yet. Back to the floor." -> floor.hub

@node floor.gully.wade
place: gully
cost: 3
do: damp_wet = 1; wet(0.5); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: The water takes the knees, and in the middle a good deal more. The Kit goes under and comes up streaming.
nar: The Damp in its compartment makes a sound like a man drowning politely.
inst: THE DAMP: Saturated. I was a man's hair once, and he was never dry either. A fire, when you have a moment.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.dry
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.4); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: The assessor crosses with the Kit held up in both arms, feet wide, face upstream, and comes out wet to the waist and dry above.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.dunk
place: gully
cost: 4
do: damp_wet = 1; wet(0.9); meter(cold, 2); offer(m.level)
nar: Two steps in, the bed moves, and the assessor sits down in the gully, Kit and all, like a statue of Patience on a fountain.
nar: On the near bank Lugg makes a sound that, in a man who spoke aloud, would be a laugh.
inst: THE DAMP: Saturated. I would like it known that I was against this.
voice: pride: Do not stand up quickly. Stand up as if you had meant to sit down. It is the only dignity left. {dc: 3}
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.rope
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.35); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: Hand over hand on Lugg's rope. Halfway, it goes taut behind: Lugg has leaned his whole height back on it.
nar: The assessor is wet to the waist. The Damp is dry, and surprised about it.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.waders
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.05); meter(cold, 1)
nar: In Merrow's waders the gully is a cold pressure on the legs and nothing more.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.hook
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.4); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: The boathook goes in upstream at every step, a third leg, and the assessor arrives wet to the waist with the Kit dry.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.bar
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.2); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The shingle bar is where she said, a hand's width of stone under the brown. Knee-deep the whole way.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.closed
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The gully is full and climbing. The drowned lamp leans on the far side. {when: clock < 23:52}
nar: In its hole a lantern still burns. {when: clock < 23:52 & has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
nar: The hole is dark. Whatever burned there tonight has been taken home. {when: clock < 23:52 & !has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
go: floor.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- beat 15: the drowned lamp
@node floor.drowned
place: drowned
alt: floor.drowned.forced ? clock >= 23:49
alt: floor.merrow.first ? clock < 23:40 & !has(met.merrow)
alt: floor.merrow.again ? clock < 23:40
alt: floor.drowned.empty ? clock >= 23:40
go: floor.drowned.empty

@node floor.merrow.first
place: drowned
cost: 4
do: set(met.merrow)
nar: The drowned lamp leans out of the mud like a tooth. In a hole in its base a lantern hangs on a nail, burning low.
nar: A short, wide man backs out of the hole with a sack that clanks, a cold pipe in his teeth and water to his thighs. He looks at the assessor. He does not ask a question.
line: MERROW: The Board sent you.
line: LAMB: The Shelf sent me. The Board sent for me.
line: MERROW: Same tide.
voice: precedent: Salvage from a wreck is salvage. Salvage from a building the sea has not finished with is called theft in most places, and in Gullet, the harbourmaster says, rope. {dc: 5}
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.drowned.creep
place: gully
cost: 4
do: damp_wet = 1; wet(0.5); meter(cold, 1); meter(dread, 1)
nar: Lantern out. The assessor wades by the sound of the water to the seaward side of the tower.
check: "[THE DARK] Get close enough to watch him, and stay out of the light." -> floor.drowned.watch / floor.drowned.seen {skill: dark, dc: 6, verb: hide, noise: 0.3}
opt: "Give it up and walk round into his light." -> floor.drowned

@node floor.drowned.watch
place: drowned
cost: 5
do: set(merrow.wet_thigh)
nar: Merrow works without looking: down into the black water at the bottom of the tower, to the thigh; up; wire into the sack.
nar: Once he stops at the nail, strikes a match, and watches it burn down to his fingers.
opt: "Step into his light." -> floor.merrow.watched
opt: "Back away into the fog, unseen." -> floor.gully.back {verb: hide, noise: 0.2}

@node floor.merrow.watched
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(met.merrow)
nar: He turns the lantern on the assessor and looks for a while.
line: MERROW: Shelf watches. Board hangs. Same tide.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.drowned.seen
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(met.merrow); rep(lowco, -1)
nar: A stone turns underfoot. The lantern swings round, and the assessor is in it, crouched, wet to the chest.
line: MERROW: Board sends spies now. In the Shelf's coat.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.again
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: Merrow sits on the rubble with the sack between his boots. He takes the pipe out of his mouth, which is as near to a greeting as he goes.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.menu
place: drowned
alt: floor.merrow.leaves ? clock >= 23:40
opt: "Keel says you darkened Mother to bring the ferry onto the Spit." -> floor.merrow.wreck ? !seen(floor.merrow.wreck) {do: set(said.wreckers); set(heard.merrow.wreckers)}
opt: "I was on the ferry. I saw a light down here, low on the water. It turned us." -> floor.merrow.saved ? has(memory.low_light) & !has(floor.merrow_trust)
opt: "Where were you when the lamps went out?" -> floor.merrow.where ? !seen(floor.merrow.where)
opt: "Tell me where you were. All of it." -> floor.merrow.where.true ? has(floor.merrow_trust) & !has(merrow.light)
opt: "Tell me the five minutes again. Slowly." -> floor.merrow.five ? has(merrow.light) & !seen(floor.merrow.five)
opt: "Show me your watch." -> floor.merrow.watch ? has(merrow.light) & !has(floor.watch_true)
opt: "Lugg says he saw a light in the hole when the ferry turned." -> floor.merrow.lugg ? has(floor.lugg_saw) & has(merrow.light) & !seen(floor.merrow.lugg)
opt: "Read his trousers with the Damp." -> floor.merrow.damp ? var.damp_wet != 1 & !has(merrow.wet_thigh) {verb: read, noise: 0}
check: "[CARBON] Read his trousers yourself. The Damp is drowned." -> floor.merrow.cloth.ok / floor.merrow.cloth.fail ? var.damp_wet == 1 & !has(merrow.wet_thigh) {verb: read, noise: 0, skill: carbon, dc: 6}
opt: "What's in the sack?" -> floor.merrow.sack ? !seen(floor.merrow.sack)
opt: "You'll tell it to someone who's earned it. Put up your best man." -> floor.salvors.challenge ? !has(merrow.light) & !has(floor.copper_taken) & !seen(floor.salvors.challenge) {verb: carry, noise: 0.6}
opt: "Take the sack from him. It is the Trust's property." -> floor.take.copper ? !has(floor.copper_taken) & !seen(floor.take.copper) {verb: carry, noise: 0.4}
opt: "That boathook in the hole." -> floor.merrow.hook ? !has(floor.move_hookpull)
opt: "Keel talks about hanging." -> floor.merrow.rope ? seen(floor.merrow.wreck) & !seen(floor.merrow.rope)
opt: "Hang my lantern in the hole beside yours." -> floor.lantern.two ? count(i.lantern) > 0 & !has(lamp.drowned.lit) {verb: light, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Look about the base of the tower." -> floor.drowned.look
opt: "Climb up into the hole and look out." -> floor.hole {verb: climb, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Go back across the gully." -> floor.gully.back

@node floor.merrow.wreck
place: drowned
cost: 3
line: MERROW: If I wanted a ship on the Spit I'd wait for fog. Not for the Board's lamp. The Board's lamp has been half blind for years. Ask any master on the run. Green, they say. She's gone green.
line: MERROW: I said I'd see her blind. In the Brine. I'd had four. She is blind. I didn't do it.
voice: hearsay: You have just said the Board's word to the man it was made for. It will be in the Gut before you are. {dc: 4}
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.saved
place: drowned
cost: 4
do: set(floor.merrow_trust); rep(lowco, 1); seenas_lowco = witness; set(said.ferry_light); set(heard.merrow.ferry_light)
nar: The assessor tells him: the dark where Mother should have been, the light low on the water, the wheel going over.
nar: Merrow takes the cold pipe out of his teeth and looks into the bowl.
line: MERROW: Nobody honest sleeps at low water. That's when the sea shows you what it took.
line: MERROW: I didn't see a ship. I saw a light on the water going the wrong way. Then it went the right way. I took that for the sea's business.
voice: undertow: He wants it to have been his lantern. {dc: 6}
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.where
place: drowned
cost: 2
line: MERROW: Asleep on my boat.
nar: His boat is on its side a quarter of a mile away. The assessor writes down "asleep on boat".
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.where.true
place: drowned
cost: 4
do: set(merrow.light); quest(a1.lowlight, merrow)
line: MERROW: All right. On the floor from just after ten. Waited at the gully for it to open. Over at sixteen past, shin-deep. Ferris on the rope.
line: MERROW: Climbing in, I knocked the lantern on the lip. There. Out. Eighteen past. Sat in the dark in there with a wet box of matches. Seven matches. Lit it again at twenty-five past and hung it on that nail so I could see what I was stealing.
line: MERROW: That's the truth and it hangs me either way. Copper off Trust property, or a false light on the rock.
nar: The assessor writes down eighteen and twenty-five, and draws a line between them.
opt: "Write the ferry's turn on the line." -> floor.gap ? has(memory.low_light) & !seen(floor.gap)
opt: "Close the Daybook." -> floor.merrow.menu

# Page 7: the five minutes no lantern burned. The gap stays open.
@node floor.gap
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: quest(a1.lowlight, gap)
if: !has(floor.page_gap) => xp(1); set(floor.page_gap)
nar: The ferry: twenty past by the true clock, twenty-four by the ship's, which runs fast.
voice: sum: Eighteen. Twenty. Twenty-five. There is no remainder. That is what is wrong with it. {dc: 4}
voice: sum: The numbers will not come out. {below: 4}
line: MERROW: Sea's business.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.five
place: drowned
cost: 4
line: MERROW: Lantern in my left hand, right on the lip. Lip's slimy. Lantern hits the stone. Glass holds. Flame doesn't.
line: MERROW: Dark like the inside of a boot. Box is wet. First match, nothing. Second, a spit. Third, I drop.
line: MERROW: Out on the water the bell, and the engine going astern, and her whole side groaning round. I'm facing the wall, striking matches. I don't see a thing.
line: MERROW: Seventh match takes. I light up. I look out the hole, and she's going away, stern light, the right way. That's all.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.watch
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(floor.watch_true)
nar: Merrow takes a brass watch on a bootlace from inside his jersey and holds it out without letting go of the lace.
line: MERROW: Set by the harbour office clock. Every Low Night. Board's clock. Only honest thing the Board owns.
inst: THE ALMANAC: His watch agrees with my dial to the minute, and my dial takes its time from the moon. I have never been so annoyed to agree with a salvor.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.lugg
place: drowned
cost: 3
line: MERROW: Ferris has eyes like a heron. Ferris saw a light.
line: MERROW: Mine was out. I had seven matches and a wet box and a ship going by I couldn't see.
line: MERROW: Both true. Write that in your book, and see does it balance.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.damp
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(merrow.wet_thigh)
read: damp merrow.trousers
inst: THE DAMP: Wet to the thigh, and the top of it fresher than the bottom. He crossed shallow and has been in deeper water since, down in the bottom of that tower. Boats are dry on the inside. Usually.
line: MERROW: Copper's at the bottom. Water's at the bottom. That's how it is with copper.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.cloth.ok
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(merrow.wet_thigh)
nar: The assessor looks, with the lantern held low and the frankness the profession requires: at the shin a tide-line dried to salt, at the thigh one still running.
line: MERROW: Copper's at the bottom. Water's at the bottom.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.cloth.fail
place: drowned
cost: 2
nar: The assessor looks at a man's trousers in the dark for some seconds, and learns that they are wet.
line: MERROW: They're wet. Sea's wet.
voice: pride: You have been staring at a salvor's legs. He will tell Lugg. Lugg will whisper it. It will lose nothing in the whispering. {dc: 4}
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.sack
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: offer(m.copper)
nar: In the sack: old wire as thick as a finger, gone green, and the curved bones of something that once turned a great lens.
line: MERROW: Copper doesn't care who owns it. Copper's a better citizen than most.
line: MERROW: Hundred and forty years it sat in there. Trust never came for it. Now it'll pay for a winter.
voice: precedent: Hound Rock is Trust property. 0441/R: the Rendle bank's nightwatchman took things nobody had counted for thirty years, and was hanged for the counting. {dc: 6}
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.rope
place: drowned
cost: 3
nar: At the word the coil of rope on his shoulder seems to grow heavier. He does not touch it.
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Ask him nothing. Wait for him to say it." -> floor.merrow.rope.ok / floor.merrow.rope.fail {skill: condolence, dc: 6}
opt: "Leave it alone." -> floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.rope.ok
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: rep(lowco, 1)
line: MERROW: Sixty years since Gullet hanged a man. Keel talks about it like a spring tide. Due, he says. Overdue.
line: MERROW: My grandfather saw the last one. Said the man's boots came off. Said that was the worst of it, the boots, and everybody looking at them.
nar: Merrow looks at his boots, which are full of the sea.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.rope.fail
place: drowned
cost: 1
line: MERROW: Rope's for boats.
nar: He lays the coil on the rubble between them, where neither of them looks at it.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.lantern.two
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(floor.lantern_two); project(l.drowned)
nar: The assessor hangs the Shelf's lantern on a second nail beside Merrow's. By double light, the stones round the hole turn out to have been painted green once.
line: MERROW: Two lights. Somebody'll think it's a church.
line: MERROW: I'll leave yours when I go. Mine goes with me. A man doesn't cross the gully in the dark.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.leaves
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(floor.merrow_left)
nar: Merrow looks at the watch on its bootlace.
line: MERROW: Twenty to. Water's coming. It doesn't wait for the Shelf.
nar: He shoulders the sack. {when: !has(floor.copper_taken)}
nar: He leaves the sack at the assessor's feet. {when: has(floor.copper_taken)}
nar: He takes his own lantern. The assessor's stays. {when: has(floor.lantern_two)}
nar: He lifts his lantern off its nail, and the hole goes dark, as if the Old Light had shut its eye. {when: !has(floor.lantern_two)}
line: MERROW: Spare waders in the hole, on the left. Take them. Give them back at the Brine. {when: has(floor.merrow_trust) & count(c.waders) == 0}
if: has(floor.merrow_trust) & count(c.waders) == 0 => give(c.waders)
nar: He steps down into the gully without testing it.
opt: "Sink it here, with a cork on a line. The Lamplighters are at the top of the steps." -> floor.copper.sink ? has(floor.merrow_trust) & !has(floor.copper_taken) & count(s.cork) > 0 {verb: rig, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Go with him, now, in his wake." -> floor.gully.back {do: set(floor.with_merrow)}
opt: "Stay a minute more." -> floor.drowned.empty

@node floor.copper.sink
place: gully
cost: 4
nar: Merrow lowers the sack into the gully by its neck, behind the tower. {when: !has(floor.copper_taken)}
nar: The assessor lowers the sack into the gully behind the tower. {when: has(floor.copper_taken)}
check: "[SUM] Cut the float line for high water, not for now." -> floor.copper.sink.ok / floor.copper.sink.fail {skill: sum, dc: 5, verb: mark, noise: 0}

@node floor.copper.sink.ok
place: gully
cost: 2
do: set(floor.copper_sunk); take(s.cork); copper = hidden; quest(a1.copper, hidden)
if: count(i.copper_sack) > 0 => take(i.copper_sack)
nar: The line is cut for five metres of tide and a fathom over. The cork sits on the brown water, a full stop.
line: MERROW: Second water. We'll want a boat. {when: !has(floor.copper_taken)}
go: floor.drowned.empty

@node floor.copper.sink.fail
place: gully
cost: 2
do: set(floor.copper_sunk); set(floor.cork_short); take(s.cork); copper = hidden; quest(a1.copper, hidden)
if: count(i.copper_sack) > 0 => take(i.copper_sack)
nar: The line is cut for the water as it is. At high water the cork will be a fathom under.
line: MERROW: Short. We'll find it at the next low. Or the eels will. {when: !has(floor.copper_taken)}
go: floor.drowned.empty

@node floor.drowned.empty
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: The drowned lamp, with nobody in it.
inst: THE ALMANAC: Back across now, or swim later. The base goes under at eight minutes to twelve and it does not go under slowly.
opt: "Hang my lantern in the hole before the water comes." -> floor.lantern.leave ? count(i.lantern) > 0 & !has(lamp.drowned.lit) {verb: light, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Sink the sack in the gully behind the tower, with a cork on a line." -> floor.copper.sink ? count(i.copper_sack) > 0 & count(s.cork) > 0 & !has(floor.copper_sunk) {verb: rig, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Look about the base of the tower." -> floor.drowned.look
opt: "Climb up into the hole and look out." -> floor.hole {verb: climb, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Go back across the gully." -> floor.gully.back

@node floor.lantern.leave
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: project(l.drowned)
nar: The Old Light is lit again, by a Shelf storm lantern with about twenty minutes of paraffin in it, which is more than it has had from anyone official in a hundred and twelve years.
go: floor.drowned.empty

@node floor.drowned.look
place: drowned
cost: 2
nar: The base is dressed stone, each block the size of a coffin, with two rusted hinge-pins where there was once a door.
voice: carbon: There was a door here. People knocked. The sea came up the steps to meet them, a little higher every year, and one year it did not go down. {dc: 6}
nar: Copper ends lie where Merrow trimmed his load, bright at the cut. {when: !has(floor.salv.wire)}
nar: A brass collar is still bolted to the old turning gear, low in the hole. {when: tide < -0.3 & !has(floor.salv.brass)}
nar: High in the base there is a niche with a locker in it. {when: !has(floor.salv.wick)}
opt: "Gather up the copper ends." -> floor.salv.wire ? !has(floor.salv.wire) {verb: salvage, noise: 0.1}
check: "[GRIP] Prise the brass collar off the gear." -> floor.salv.brass.ok / floor.salv.brass.fail ? tide < -0.3 & !has(floor.salv.brass) {verb: pry, noise: 0.3, skill: grip, dc: 5}
opt: "Open the locker in the niche." -> floor.salv.wick ? !has(floor.salv.wick) {verb: pry, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Look down into the black water at the bottom of the tower." -> floor.conger ? !has(floor.salv.crown) & !seen(floor.conger.leave) & clock < 23:48 {verb: read, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Leave the stones alone." -> floor.drowned

@node floor.salv.wire
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(floor.salv.wire); give(s.copper_wire)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.copper_wire)
nar: The assessor pockets the offcuts, green outside and bright as a new penny at the cut.
line: MERROW: Take them. Offcuts. Copper doesn't mind who. {when: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow)}
go: floor.drowned.look

@node floor.salv.brass.ok
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: set(floor.salv.brass); give(s.brass); wet(0.1)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.brass)
nar: The collar comes away. Heavy brass, gold where the thumb rubs it.
go: floor.drowned.look

@node floor.salv.brass.fail
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: wet(0.2); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The collar does not move. The assessor does, backward, into knee-deep water.
line: MERROW: Twist. Not pull. Brass is like the Board. {when: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow)}
go: floor.drowned.look

@node floor.salv.wick
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(floor.salv.wick); give(s.wick)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.wick)
nar: A tin of lamp-wick, gone to felt at the outer turns and good at the heart. A keeper put it here against a long night, and the long night came, and it was the sea's.
go: floor.drowned.look

@node floor.hole
place: drowned
cost: 3
nar: Inside, the hole is a stone throat with water in the bottom, and by the nail a fresh black kiss of soot where a lantern struck.
nar: Outward lies the bay: the channel, the Spit, the water where the ferry came in. {when: clock < 23:20}
nar: Outward there is fog, and nothing in it. {when: clock >= 23:20}
nar: Mother's beam goes over, green, and for an instant the inside of the Old Light is lit. {when: mother == burning}
alt: floor.gap ? has(merrow.light) & has(memory.low_light) & !seen(floor.gap)
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.drowned.forced
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: The water comes over the rubble in small decided waves, each an inch further, like a clerk filling in a form.
inst: THE ALMANAC: The base goes under at eight minutes to twelve. You are standing on the base. I make no further comment.
go: floor.gully.back

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the gully: crossing back
@node floor.gully.back
place: gully
alt: floor.gully.run ? clock >= 23:30
cost: 1
nar: The gully going back is the gully coming out, only the assessor is colder and the water has had longer to think.
opt: "Wade straight across." -> floor.gully.back.wade {verb: wade, noise: 0.3}
check: "[BALLAST] Wade back with the Kit held high." -> floor.gully.back.dry / floor.gully.back.dunk {verb: wade, noise: 0.2, skill: ballast, dc: 5}
opt: "Cross back on Lugg's rope." -> floor.gully.back.rope ? (seen(floor.lugg.lee) | guise == floor) & !has(said.lugg_refused) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Wade back in Merrow's waders." -> floor.gully.back.waders ? worn(c.waders) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Back along your hand line." -> floor.gully.back.rope ? has(floor.handline) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Not yet." -> floor.drowned

@node floor.gully.back.wade
place: gully
cost: 3
do: damp_wet = 1; wet(0.5); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: The assessor crosses to the waist, with the Kit under for a long count of three.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.gully.back.dry
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.4); meter(cold, 1); offer(m.level)
nar: Across with the Kit held high, wet to the waist and still, in the upper half, a credit to the Shelf.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.gully.back.dunk
place: gully
cost: 4
do: damp_wet = 1; wet(0.9); meter(cold, 2); offer(m.level)
nar: Halfway, the soft place. The assessor comes up the far bank on all fours with the dignity of a seal that has been asked to leave.
inst: THE DAMP: Saturated. I was a man's hair once. I was never this.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.gully.back.rope
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.35); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The assessor crosses back on Lugg's rope. At the near bank a long hand lifts the assessor by the collar and sets the assessor down.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.gully.back.waders
place: gully
cost: 3
do: wet(0.05); meter(cold, 1)
nar: Back across in Merrow's waders, which slap and suck and keep the sea out with an air of doing it as a personal favour.
go: floor.hub

# The run: leaving the drowned lamp after 23:30 (r.gully). Fallback per LWD1-FORMAT 5.8.
@node floor.gully.run
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The gully is the sea now, waist-deep in the middle and rising.
nar: Merrow is in it ahead, the sack on his shoulder. {when: has(floor.with_merrow)}
go: floor.eels.choose

@node floor.gully.go
place: gully
alt: floor.gully.fallback ? var.runs == 0
cost: 1
do: run(r.gully)

@node floor.gully.fallback
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The water is waist-deep in the middle, and the steps are lanterns in the fog.
check: "[KNEES] Wade for the steps." -> floor.run.gully.win / floor.run.gully.lose ? clock < 23:42 & !has(floor.with_merrow) {verb: wade, noise: 0.4, skill: knees, dc: 6, red}
check: "[KNEES] Wade for the steps. It is past the waist in the middle." -> floor.run.gully.win / floor.run.gully.lose ? clock >= 23:42 & !has(floor.with_merrow) {verb: wade, noise: 0.4, skill: knees, dc: 7, red}
check: "[KNEES] Wade for the steps in Merrow's wake, where he breaks the water." -> floor.run.gully.win / floor.run.gully.lose ? has(floor.with_merrow) {verb: wade, noise: 0.4, skill: knees, dc: 5, red}
check: "[GRIP] Go hand over hand along your line on the ribs." -> floor.run.gully.win / floor.run.gully.lose ? has(floor.handline) {skill: grip, dc: 4, red}

@node floor.run.gully.win
place: steps
cost: 2
do: wet(0.5); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The assessor comes up out of the gully, crosses the floor, and sits down on the second step without having decided to.
nar: Merrow, three steps up, sets the sack down and nods once. {when: has(floor.with_merrow)}
line: MERROW: You'll do. {when: has(floor.with_merrow)}
nar: Out over the gully a small light burns low in the Old Light. A woman on the steps makes a sign the assessor does not know. {when: has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
opt: "Go back down onto the floor while it lasts." -> floor.hub ? tide < -0.27
opt: "Climb the steps to the quay." -> quay.hub +2

@node floor.run.gully.lose
place: steps
cost: 20
do: wet(1); damp_wet = 1; meter(cold, 3); rep(lowco, 1)
if: count(c.shelf_hat) > 0 => take(c.shelf_hat); set(floor.hat_lost)
if: !has(floor.hat_lost) & count(i.lantern) > 0 => take(i.lantern); set(floor.lantern_lost)
nar: In the middle of the gully the bottom goes, and the assessor goes with it, sideways.
nar: Merrow's hand closes on the collar from upstream. He walks the assessor out with the sack on his other shoulder. {when: clock >= 23:40}
nar: A loop of rope comes taut across the assessor's chest. Lugg brings the assessor in to the steps. {when: clock < 23:40}
nar: The Shelf bowler is out on the water, upright, going away toward the Spit like a small official who has remembered an appointment. {when: has(floor.hat_lost)}
nar: The lantern is gone, lit for a moment under the brown water, and then not. {when: has(floor.lantern_lost)}
line: MERROW: You'll want the fire. {when: clock >= 23:40}
inst: THE DAMP: Saturated. I have been in the sea before, once, with Assessor Pollard. He also said it was nothing.
opt: "Climb to the quay and find a fire." -> quay.hub +2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- beat 14: the fish
@node floor.fish.first
place: fish
cost: 3
do: quest(a1.fish, met)
nar: The fish is the size of a small cart with the horse included, on its side in a scour too shallow for it. Its one upward eye, the size of a dinner plate, looks at the sky with enormous, patient surprise.
nar: Every half-minute its gill lifts, and lets go.
nar: Round it stand the claimants: a girl with a slate, an old woman with a gaff, a boy chalking on its flank, and a sign with a candle.
voice: smell: Cold iron. Deep water. A church cellar. It has come up from somewhere fish do not usually discuss. {dc: 4}
inst: THE ALMANAC: The channel beside it fills enough to float a cart at twenty to twelve. Before that nothing floats here but opinion.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.again
place: fish
cost: 1
alt: floor.fish.knives ? var.fish == eaten & clock >= 23:44 & !seen(floor.fish.knives)
nar: The fish lies as it was, and the children go round it. {when: clock < 23:35}
nar: The rain is on the fish and the gill lifts more easily. The rain is doing for it what nobody on the floor has yet agreed to. {when: clock >= 23:35}
nar: A candle burns at its head, and the children sit on their heels in the mud. {when: var.floor.award == congregation}
nar: The Guild's chalk mark is half washed off, and the boy has gone. {when: var.floor.award == guild | var.floor.award == lowco}
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.menu
place: fish
alt: floor.gulls.down ? clock >= 23:40 & clock < 23:48 & var.fish == stranded & var.floor.award != congregation & !seen(floor.gulls.down)
alt: floor.fish.turnsoon ? clock >= 23:40 & clock < 23:48 & var.floor.award == fish & var.fish == stranded & !seen(floor.fish.turnsoon)
opt: "Talk to the girl with the slate." -> floor.dilly.first ? !has(met.dilly)
opt: "Talk to Dilly about the book." -> floor.dilly.menu ? has(met.dilly)
opt: "Talk to the old woman on the bucket." -> floor.cockle.first ? !has(met.cockle) & !has(floor.cockle_home)
opt: "Talk to Nan Cockle." -> floor.cockle.menu ? has(met.cockle) & !has(floor.cockle_home)
opt: "Talk to the boy in the apron." -> floor.runner ? var.floor.award == none & !seen(floor.runner.shake.ok) & !seen(floor.runner.shake.fail)
opt: "Read the sign at the fish's head." -> floor.sign ? !seen(floor.sign) {verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Look the fish in the eye." -> floor.fish.eye {verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Open a claim on the fish." -> floor.fish.claim ? var.floor.award == none & var.fish == stranded & seen(floor.runner) & seen(floor.sign) & has(met.cockle)
check: "[SUM] Send the children for the long spar and set them on it by height." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.fish.spar.fail ? clock >= 23:40 & var.floor.award == fish & var.fish == stranded {skill: sum, dc: 6, verb: carry, noise: 0.4}
opt: "Help the children turn the fish into the channel." -> floor.fish.turn ? var.floor.award == fish & var.fish == stranded {verb: carry, noise: 0.4}
opt: "Dig a cut to her tail off the channel, with the children." -> floor.fish.dig ? var.floor.award == fish & var.fish == stranded & clock < 23:40 & !has(floor.channel_dug) +8 {verb: rig, noise: 0.3}
opt: "Wait with the fish for the channel to fill." -> floor.fish.wait ? var.floor.award == fish & var.fish == stranded & clock < 23:40 +5 {verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Leave the fish." -> floor.hub

@node floor.fish.eye
place: fish
cost: 2
nar: The eye is a lens as deep as a bowl. Every lantern on the floor stands in it, small and upside down.
nar: Mother's beam comes round, and the eye gives back a green flash out of the mud. {when: mother == burning}
inst: CANDLEMAS: A very fine lens. I have known lighthouses with worse. I see why the Congregation is interested.
voice: salt: It has until the water, and the water is late for it. The gill is slower than it was. Call it the half-hour, and not the whole of that. {dc: 5, when: clock < 23:35}
voice: salt: The rain has bought it time. Not much. The rain is a loan. {dc: 5, when: clock >= 23:35}
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.dig
place: fish
cost: 1
do: set(floor.channel_dug); wet(0.3); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The children and the assessor cut a ditch from the channel to the fish's tail. At twenty-five to, water comes along it, and the tail moves once.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.spar.fail
place: fish
cost: 3
nar: The tallest go at the thin end and the smallest at the fulcrum, which is the wrong way round. Eleven children sit down in the mud. The fish has not moved.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.wait
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: The channel fills by a finger's width, and then another. The children wait too, with the stillness of people who expect to be sent home.
go: floor.fish.menu

# ---- Dilly Rudd and the book
@node floor.dilly.first
place: fish
cost: 3
do: set(met.dilly)
nar: The girl is Dilly Rudd, about ten, with a face like a clenched fist that has been told a joke. She runs the only book on Low Night.
line: DILLY: You're the Shelf. Lives is fours. Dies is evens. Gulls is threes. Guild knives is fives, and I want it said I never took Agnes Spratt's money.
line: DILLY: We call her the Alderman. Same mouth.
nar: The fish's mouth is wide, downturned and lipless. The assessor declines to give a professional opinion.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.menu
place: fish
opt: "Who has bet on what?" -> floor.dilly.book ? !has(floor.dilly_book)
check: "[THE CHIT] Read her slate upside down while she talks." -> floor.dilly.slate.ok / floor.dilly.slate.fail ? !has(floor.dilly_book) {skill: chit, dc: 5}
opt: "A chit on lives." -> floor.dilly.bet.lives ? var.floor.bet == none & count(i.chits) > 0 {do: floor.bet = lives; take(i.chits, 1)}
opt: "A chit on dies." -> floor.dilly.bet.dies ? var.floor.bet == none & count(i.chits) > 0 {do: floor.bet = dies; take(i.chits, 1)}
opt: "Why don't you turn it yourselves?" -> floor.dilly.why ? has(floor.dilly_book) & !seen(floor.dilly.why)
opt: "Leave the book alone." -> floor.fish.menu

@node floor.dilly.book
place: fish
cost: 2
line: DILLY: Everybody's on dies. Everybody's sensible. Twenty-two of them, a farthing up to a ha'penny, and Wat Gedge put his knife on it, which I'm holding.
line: DILLY: Dies pays evens. That's the book.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.slate.ok
place: fish
cost: 2
do: set(floor.dilly_book)
nar: Upside down, the slate is clear. Every line is a bet on dies, taken at evens. At the foot, rubbed out once and written again: D. RUDD, LIVES, 1s. 4d. Every coin Dilly Rudd owns, and possibly some of her mother's.
nar: Dilly turns the slate round.
line: DILLY: Slate's private. Like confession.
line: DILLY: A book that touches the horse isn't a book. Everybody knows. I can't turn her. Nobody that's bet can turn her. That's rules.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.slate.fail
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: Dilly, without looking, tilts the slate exactly as far the other way. She has been read upside down by better.
line: DILLY: Bets are a ha'penny to look. A penny to read.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.why
place: fish
cost: 3
line: DILLY: Anybody on the book can't touch the horse. That's everybody on the floor under twelve.
line: DILLY: Grown-ups won't. Guild wants her for the stall. Nan wants her for the Company. The candle people want her to lie there and be holy at.
line: DILLY: You're not on the book. Unless you've bet. Have you bet?
line: DILLY: Channel's deep enough at twenty to. Takes a spar and all of us pushing and one grown-up that's allowed. And somebody to say who she belongs to, so the Guild boy doesn't run for the knives.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.bet.lives
place: fish
cost: 1
line: DILLY: Fours. On lives. You're the only grown-up that has.
nar: She writes it down.
go: floor.dilly.menu

@node floor.dilly.bet.dies
place: fish
cost: 1
line: DILLY: Evens. Same as everybody.
nar: She writes it down without looking up, and the assessor joins twenty-two children and a man called Wat Gedge in having bet against the fish.
go: floor.dilly.menu

# ---- Nan Cockle
@node floor.cockle.first
place: fish
cost: 3
do: set(met.cockle)
nar: Nan Cockle of the Low Company, eighty-one, in oilskins gone soft as a glove, the gaff across her knees. She looks the assessor up and down and settles on the boots, the only part she thinks worth a judgement.
line: COCKLE: Sit down, child. No, not on that. That's mine too.
line: COCKLE: This fish is the Company's. What the tide leaves, the Company lifts. Five low Low Nights I've seen, and it's been so at every one.
line: COCKLE: Ferris says you've been saying wreckers. Words float, child. You'd be surprised what comes in on the next tide. {when: has(said.wreckers)}
go: floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.menu
place: fish
opt: "What will the Company do with a fish this size?" -> floor.cockle.use ? !seen(floor.cockle.use)
opt: "Have you ever been out to the Old Light yourself?" -> floor.cockle.door ? !seen(floor.cockle.door)
opt: "You walk this mud as if it were a floor." -> floor.cockle.mud ? !has(floor.move_mudstep)
opt: "Show me the way across to the Old Light." -> floor.cockle.guide ? tide < -0.35 & clock < 23:40 & !has(floor.cockle_guided) & !has(floor.bar_told)
opt: "The water's coming. Let me walk you to the steps." -> floor.cockle.home ? clock >= 23:25 & !has(floor.cockle_home) +6 {verb: carry, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Leave her to her bucket." -> floor.fish.menu

@node floor.cockle.use
place: fish
cost: 2
line: COCKLE: Sell her to the Guild by the pound, if they'd pay, which they won't, because they say she's theirs. Render her for lamp oil, if I had a pot, which I haven't.
line: COCKLE: Or sit here till the tide takes her, and say I claimed her. A claim's a claim. Even when it's wet.
go: floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.door
place: fish
cost: 3
line: COCKLE: Once. My first low one. I was five, on my father's shoulders. It had a door then. Green paint.
line: COCKLE: I knocked on it.
line: COCKLE: Another time, child. When I've a fire and a drink and somebody's paying.
go: floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.guide
place: fish
cost: 2
line: COCKLE: There's a bar. Shingle, under the brown. Knee-deep where the gully's chest-deep. The Company's known it since before my first low one, and the Board never asked.
line: COCKLE: I'll show you for a chit. I'm too old for favours on account.
line: COCKLE: You've the floor on you, though. Oilskin and mud. That's fare enough. {when: guise == floor}
opt: "Show me, then." -> floor.cockle.cross ? guise == floor
opt: "A chit, then." -> floor.cockle.cross ? count(i.chits) > 0 {do: take(i.chits, 1)}
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Ask her when she last stood at the Old Light." -> floor.cockle.cross / floor.cockle.guide.fail {skill: condolence, dc: 6}
opt: "Another time." -> floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.guide.fail
place: fish
cost: 1
do: set(floor.bar_told)
line: COCKLE: Don't go soft on me, child. I've been sold softer things by the Board.
line: COCKLE: Find it yourself. It starts where the gulls stand in the water.
go: floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.cross
place: gully
cost: 8
do: set(floor.cockle_guided); set(floor.bar_told); wet(0.2); meter(cold, 1)
nar: Nan Cockle goes into the gully at a slant nobody would choose, and the water comes only to her knees. The assessor follows her exact steps.
nar: On the far side she lays a hand on one of the rusted hinge-pins, the way you touch a horse you used to own, and goes back alone.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.cockle.home
place: steps
cost: 1
do: set(floor.cockle_home); set(floor.move_mudstep); tab_cockle = 1; rep(lowco, 1)
nar: Nan Cockle takes the assessor's arm without comment, and the bucket and the gaff. The walk takes six minutes.
nar: On the way she teaches the mud-step.
line: COCKLE: Foot flat, child. Let the mud have it. Never the heel first. {when: !has(floor.move_mudstep)}
line: COCKLE: Truth is, I'd sooner it went home. The fish. Don't tell the Company. The Company is me and Tub and Ferris, and Tub and Ferris would laugh.
line: COCKLE: You're on my slate now, child. That's a good slate to be on. Ask Sabine. {when: clock < 23:48}
opt: "Go back down to the floor." -> floor.hub ? tide < -0.27
opt: "Climb to the quay." -> quay.hub +2

# ---- the Guild's runner and the Congregation's sign
@node floor.runner
place: fish
cost: 3
nar: The boy is Gill, Agnes Spratt's runner. He speaks only in Mrs Spratt's words.
line: GILL: Mrs Spratt says all fish is Guild. Mrs Spratt says this is a fish. Mrs Spratt says the knives come at the turn of the floor.
nar: His chalk mark on the fish's flank is a fish inside a ring. It looks like an eye.
opt: "Did Marrow Dunlin send you?" -> floor.runner.marrow ? !seen(floor.runner.marrow)
check: "[GRIP] Lift him off the mud by his apron straps until he says something of his own." -> floor.runner.shake.ok / floor.runner.shake.fail ? !has(vote.older) {skill: grip, dc: 6, verb: carry, noise: 0.5}
opt: "Leave him to his chalk." -> floor.fish.menu

@node floor.runner.marrow
place: fish
cost: 2
line: GILL: Mr Dunlin didn't send me. Mrs Spratt did. Mrs Spratt says that's the same thing, near enough, and will be more so by Lady Day.
nar: He says this with no idea of what it means, and the assessor writes it down with some idea.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.runner.shake.ok
place: fish
cost: 2
do: set(vote.older); quest(a1.vote, older); rep(guild, -1)
nar: Gill comes up off the mud by his apron straps, boots pedalling.
line: GILL: Mrs Spratt had me fetch yesterday's smoked one from Shadwell's for the pans. She said in the dark nobody'd know a day.
nar: Set down, he goes white, and goes.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.runner.shake.fail
place: fish
cost: 2
do: rep(guild, -1)
nar: Gill drops out of the apron like a peeled shrimp and runs. In the apron pocket: a smokehouse ticket, SHADWELL, 1 SMOKED, and a day the rain has taken.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.sign
place: fish
cost: 2
nar: The sign:
nar: THIS CREATURE BEARS THE EYE. LET NO KNIFE OPEN WHAT THE LORD HAS NOT OPENED. VIGIL KEPT FROM THE STEPS. THE CONGREGATION OF THE FILAMENT.
nar: A candle in a jam jar at its foot. Up on the steps, a dozen bell jars face this way.
voice: smallprint: Turn it over. The other side is an old Municipal notice, LAMP QUAY, SODIUM WORKS IN PROGRESS, THE MUNICIPAL REGRETS ANY INCONVENIENCE TO COLOUR. The Congregation has painted its claim on the back of the Trust. {dc: 4, when: light >= 0.1}
voice: smallprint: Too dark to read the back, and the front is all capitals, which are a kind of shouting. {when: light < 0.1}
go: floor.fish.menu

# ---- the little claim inside the big one
@node floor.fish.claim
place: fish
cost: 4
do: quest(a1.fish, claims)
nar: The assessor writes at the top of a fresh page: CLAIM 4471/G, SCHEDULE F. Nature of loss: a fish. Claimants: three.
nar: The children stop circling.
line: LAMB: Three parties claim this fish: the Guild, by Mrs Spratt; the Low Company, by Mrs Cockle; the Congregation, by notice. I will hear any further statements now.
line: COCKLE: Five low ones. The Company's had the floor at every one.
line: GILL: Mrs Spratt says it's Guild.
opt: "Find for the Guild. All fish is Guild." -> floor.rule.guild {do: set(said.fish_guild); set(heard.cockle.fish_guild); set(heard.dilly.fish_guild)}
opt: "Find for the Low Company. The floor is theirs." -> floor.rule.lowco {do: set(said.fish_lowco); set(heard.cockle.fish_lowco); set(heard.dilly.fish_lowco)}
opt: "Find for the Congregation. No knife." -> floor.rule.congregation {do: set(said.fish_congregation); set(heard.cockle.fish_congregation); set(heard.dilly.fish_congregation)}
check: "[PRECEDENT] Find that no claimant has an interest. The fish holds title to itself." -> floor.rule.fish.ok / floor.rule.fish.fail {skill: precedent, dc: 6, do: set(said.fish_itself); set(heard.cockle.fish_itself); set(heard.dilly.fish_itself)}
opt: "Decline. The Shelf does not insure fish." -> floor.rule.decline

@node floor.rule.guild
place: fish
cost: 2
do: floor.award = guild; fish = eaten; quest(a1.fish, eaten); rep(guild, 1); rep(lowco, -1); rep(congregation, -1)
nar: Gill is gone before the sentence ends, calling for knives.
line: COCKLE: Well. That's the Shelf, then.
line: DILLY: Fives. Agnes Spratt's money. I said I'd never.
nar: The children sit down in the mud.
voice: formletter: The finding was made in accordance with the Guild's long-standing practice. It is regretted that the fish was not consulted. {dc: 4}
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.rule.lowco
place: fish
cost: 3
do: floor.award = lowco; fish = eaten; quest(a1.fish, eaten); rep(lowco, 1); rep(congregation, -1)
nar: Nan Cockle receives this as her due and sells the fish to Gill on the spot for a shilling and a bucket of the liver.
line: COCKLE: Claimed and sold. That's how it's done, child.
nar: Three claims went into the Daybook. One sale came out. Gill runs for the knives.
line: DILLY: She'll not live, then. Fives.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.rule.congregation
place: fish
cost: 2
do: floor.award = congregation; fish = gulls; quest(a1.fish, gulls); rep(congregation, 1); rep(guild, -1); rep(lowco, -1)
nar: From the steps, through the fog, Tobit Quill singing.
line: COCKLE: They'll not touch it. Nor will the gulls be told. Gulls aren't members.
nar: On the ribs, thirty-one gulls shift their feet.
voice: undertow: Nobody will cut it. Nobody will move it. You have arranged for it to die with dignity, in front of an audience, at the gulls' convenience. {dc: 5}
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.rule.fish.ok
place: fish
cost: 3
do: floor.award = fish; rep(lowco, 1); rep(guild, -1)
line: LAMB: The Shelf's practice is plain. A claimant must show an interest in the thing claimed. A thing that is still breathing has the prior interest in itself. I find that no party holds title, and that the fish does.
line: COCKLE: Five low ones, and I never heard that ruling. Fair enough.
line: GILL: Mrs Spratt will want that in writing.
nar: The assessor tears out the page. The sign says nothing, which the assessor records as consent.
line: DILLY: Then it's nobody's. Then anybody can turn her that's not on the book.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.rule.fish.fail
place: fish
cost: 3
do: floor.award = fish; set(floor.fish_contested); rep(guild, -1)
nar: The assessor argues from 1655/B, the bell at Brack, that a thing belongs to whatever it falls on.
line: COCKLE: So it's ours, then. You've just said.
line: GILL: Mrs Spratt says that's not law.
nar: Gill runs for the knives anyway. Dilly, loudly, rules for them all.
line: DILLY: The Shelf says it's hers. The fish's. Everybody heard. Anybody not on the book can turn her.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.rule.decline
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: The Shelf does not insure fish, the assessor says. The children look at the assessor the way the fish does.
line: DILLY: Then what's it for?
voice: formletter: It was explained that the matter fell outside the scope of the policy. It was not explained to anyone's satisfaction, including the assessor's. {dc: 4}
go: floor.fish.menu

# ---- turning the fish: the run (r.fish), 23:40 to 23:48
@node floor.fish.turnsoon
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: The channel is full, deep enough to float a cart, going out toward the sea.
line: DILLY: Now. It's now. Spar's under her. Everybody's here that's allowed.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.turn
place: fish
alt: floor.fish.notyet ? clock < 23:40 & !(has(floor.channel_dug) & clock >= 23:35)
alt: floor.fish.fallback ? var.runs == 0
cost: 1
nar: A spar from the Margery Dole is under the fish's back, with eleven children on it, Dilly at the end, and the assessor, who is not on the book, in the middle. {when: var.floor.bet != lives}
nar: A spar from the Margery Dole is under the fish's back, with eleven children on it. Dilly sees the assessor's chit on lives and says nothing about the horse. {when: var.floor.bet == lives}
nar: At the foot of the steps, lanterns coming down: the Guild, with knives. {when: has(floor.fish_contested)}
nar: The gulls are still on the fish. {when: seen(floor.gulls.down) & !has(floor.gulls_off)}
inst: THE ALMANAC: The floor closes at twelve minutes to. This fish is between you and the steps. Be quick, or be thorough. Not both.
do: run(r.fish)

@node floor.fish.notyet
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: The channel is a ditch with a finger of water in it.
inst: THE ALMANAC: Twenty to twelve. Not before. The sea has a timetable and it will not be hurried by a fish.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.fallback
place: fish
cost: 1
check: "[GRIP] Lever the fish over into the channel." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.run.fish.lose ? !has(floor.fish_contested) & (has(floor.gulls_off) | !seen(floor.gulls.down)) {verb: pry, noise: 0.3, skill: grip, dc: 6, red}
check: "[GRIP] Lever the fish over into the channel, gulls and all." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.run.fish.lose ? !has(floor.fish_contested) & seen(floor.gulls.down) & !has(floor.gulls_off) {verb: pry, noise: 0.3, skill: grip, dc: 7, red}
check: "[GRIP] Lever her over with the boathook, hook under the gill-plate." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.run.fish.lose ? count(w.boathook) > 0 {skill: grip, dc: 5, red, verb: pry, noise: 0.3}
check: "[GRIP] Roll her down the cut you dug." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.run.fish.lose ? has(floor.channel_dug) {skill: grip, dc: 5, red, verb: carry, noise: 0.3}
check: "[GRIP] Lever the fish over into the channel before the knives come." -> floor.run.fish.win / floor.run.fish.lose ? has(floor.fish_contested) {verb: pry, noise: 0.3, skill: grip, dc: 7, red}

@node floor.run.fish.win
place: fish
cost: 3
do: fish = turned; quest(a1.fish, turned); tab_dilly = 1; wet(0.5); meter(cold, 1); rep(guild, -1)
if: var.floor.bet == lives => give(i.chits, 4)
nar: The fish goes over all at once, like a wardrobe.
nar: She moves once, the whole length of her, and the channel takes her. The great eye goes under last, still looking up.
nar: Twenty-two children who bet against it cheer. Dilly Rudd does not.
line: DILLY: You weren't on the book. I'll say so to anyone.
line: DILLY: I owe you. Not money. The other kind. You come and find me and I'll know what you want before you do.
nar: She pays the assessor out at fours from a pocket that clinks, and turns away before her face can do anything. {when: var.floor.bet == lives}
opt: "Go back up the floor." -> floor.hub ? tide < -0.27
opt: "Make for the steps." -> quay.hub +3

@node floor.run.fish.lose
place: fish
cost: 4
do: fish = gulls; quest(a1.fish, gulls); take(i.chits, 2); wet(0.6); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The spar slips. The fish rolls a foot toward the channel and a foot back.
nar: The gulls come down in the fog and stand about the fish in a ring.
nar: Dilly pays out to twenty-two children and Wat Gedge. The book pays against the assessor too: two chits.
line: DILLY: You tried. That's not nothing. It's not much.
voice: undertow: Cover her book. You have chits. She will not ask. {dc: 5}
opt: "Cover Dilly's book out of your own chits." -> floor.dilly.cover ? count(i.chits) >= 2
opt: "Leave the gulls to it." -> floor.hub ? tide < -0.27
opt: "Make for the steps." -> quay.hub +3

@node floor.dilly.cover
place: fish
cost: 2
do: take(i.chits, 2); tab_dilly = 1; set(floor.dilly_covered)
nar: The assessor counts two chits into Dilly Rudd's hand. She looks at them for a long time.
line: DILLY: That's not the book. The book's done. That's something else.
line: DILLY: I'll know what it's for when you ask.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fish.knives
place: fish
cost: 2
nar: The Guild comes down the floor: three men in aprons, a handcart, the knives in a roll carried as respectfully as a bishop's crook.
nar: They do not look at the assessor. One of them takes his cap off to the fish.
opt: "Leave them to their work." -> floor.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Merrow coming home, 23:43 to 23:48
@node floor.merrow.returns
place: floor
cost: 2
nar: Merrow comes out of the fog over the gully with the sack on his shoulder, wet to the thigh, while Lugg hauls the rope in hand over hand.
nar: His heels go down into the mud a full inch with every step.
line: MERROW: The Board sent you. {when: !has(met.merrow)}
line: LAMB: The Shelf sent me. The Board sent for me. {when: !has(met.merrow)}
line: MERROW: Same tide. {when: !has(met.merrow)}
line: MERROW: Water's in. Shelf should be up the steps. {when: has(met.merrow)}
do: set(met.merrow)
opt: "Read his trousers as he passes." -> floor.merrow.returns.damp ? var.damp_wet != 1 & !has(merrow.wet_thigh)
opt: "I was on the ferry. I saw a light at the Old Light. It turned us." -> floor.merrow.returns.saved ? has(memory.low_light) & !has(floor.merrow_trust)
opt: "Let him go by." -> floor.hub

@node floor.merrow.returns.damp
place: floor
cost: 1
do: set(merrow.wet_thigh)
inst: THE DAMP: Wet to the thigh, the top fresher than the bottom, and all of it fresh from the gully.
nar: Merrow does not stop, and does not ask what the brass thing is for.
go: floor.hub

@node floor.merrow.returns.saved
place: floor
cost: 3
do: set(floor.merrow_trust); rep(lowco, 1); seenas_lowco = witness; set(said.ferry_light); set(heard.merrow.ferry_light)
nar: The assessor tells it walking beside him. At the foot of the steps he sets the sack down and looks back at the fog where the Old Light is.
line: MERROW: I didn't see a ship. I saw a light on the water going the wrong way. Then it went the right way.
line: MERROW: I'll be at the Brine. By the stove. A man can say things by a stove.
go: floor.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- moves taught: the hook-pull and the mud-step
@node floor.merrow.hook
place: drowned
cost: 4
nar: The boathook leans in the hole, the hook worn bright inside its curve.
alt: floor.merrow.hook.teach ? has(floor.merrow_trust)
line: MERROW: That's my second hook. Not for lending.
line: MERROW: Tell me a true thing, Shelf. Not about me. About you. Then we'll see.
opt: "I don't know whether the Shelf still exists. Its messages come by tube. Nobody has seen an office in years." -> floor.merrow.hook.teach {do: set(said.shelf_doubt); set(heard.merrow.shelf_doubt)}
opt: "I was frightened on the ferry. I held the rail and shut my eyes, and only opened them for the light." -> floor.merrow.hook.teach {do: set(said.ferry_fear); set(heard.merrow.ferry_fear)}
opt: "Keep your hook." -> floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.merrow.hook.teach
place: drowned
cost: 4
do: give(w.boathook); set(floor.move_hookpull)
line: MERROW: That'll do. {when: has(said.shelf_doubt) | has(said.ferry_fear)}
nar: He puts the boathook in the assessor's hands and sets them on the haft from behind.
line: MERROW: Point's for keeping a thing off. Hook's for bringing it in. Hook the ankle. Don't pull with the arms. Sit back, like the tide going out. He comes with you.
line: MERROW: Hook-pull. My father's. He used it on boats. Once on a bailiff.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.cockle.mud
place: fish
cost: 3
line: COCKLE: You walk this floor like a cat on a wet roof, child. Every step a complaint.
line: COCKLE: I'll teach you, for a true thing. Something you've not told the Board.
opt: "I saw a light at the Old Light from the ferry. The town thinks it was Tub's. I am not sure it was." -> floor.cockle.mud.teach ? has(memory.low_light) {do: set(said.light_doubt); set(heard.cockle.light_doubt)}
opt: "I haven't told the Board anything. I've only listened to it drip." -> floor.cockle.mud.teach {do: set(said.board_drip); set(heard.cockle.board_drip)}
opt: "Another time." -> floor.cockle.menu

@node floor.cockle.mud.teach
place: fish
cost: 3
do: set(floor.move_mudstep)
line: COCKLE: Don't step on it. Step into it. Foot flat, let the mud have it a moment, and it'll give it back. Never the heel first.
nar: She moves sideways a yard without a sound or a splash, and back, and sits.
line: COCKLE: Mud-step. My grandmother's. The Lamplighters can't do it. Nor the Board. That's why they stop at the steps.
go: floor.cockle.menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Fray: e.salvors (set fight if Lamb takes the copper)
@node floor.take.copper
place: drowned
cost: 2
nar: The assessor takes the neck of the sack. Merrow does not let go, and does not pull.
line: MERROW: Copper doesn't care who carries it. Ferris does.
nar: Out of the fog round the tower come Lugg and two salvors with crowbars. Lugg's lips move.
opt: "Give the sack back." -> floor.salvors.giveback {verb: carry, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Merrow. Tell them to stand off." -> floor.salvors.word ? has(floor.merrow_trust)
opt: "Keep hold of it." -> floor.salvors.fight {verb: carry, noise: 0.5}

@node floor.salvors.giveback
place: drowned
cost: 1
do: rep(lowco, 1)
nar: Merrow sets the sack between his boots. The salvors go back round the tower.
line: MERROW: You'll want it in your book that you had it. Put it in.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.salvors.word
place: drowned
cost: 2
line: MERROW: Ferris. Leave it. The Shelf's putting it down.
nar: Lugg stops, and the salvors with him. The assessor finds the sack being set down, by the assessor's own hands.
line: MERROW: There. Nobody's hit anybody. That's a good night on the floor.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.salvors.fight
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: Merrow lets go and steps back against the stones with his arms folded, the way a man stands out of a quarrel between the sea and the weather.
do: clear(floor.fight_word)
if: seen(floor.drowned.watch) => fight(e.salvors.sneak)
if: !seen(floor.drowned.watch) => fight(e.salvors)

@node floor.salvors.challenge
place: drowned
cost: 2
nar: Merrow whistles once, low. Lugg comes round the tower with the two salvors.
line: MERROW: Ferris. The Shelf wants to earn something.
line: LUGG: On the rubble. Till somebody sits in the water.
opt: "On the rubble, then." -> floor.salvors.word.fight
opt: "Think better of it." -> floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.salvors.word.fight
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: The salvors set their crowbars against the stones. Lugg takes off his coat, which takes a while.
do: set(floor.fight_word); fight(e.salvors)

@node floor.fight.word.win
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: clear(floor.fight_word); set(struck.lugg); set(merrow.light); quest(a1.lowlight, merrow); seenas_lowco = witness
nar: It ends with a salvor sitting in the gully and Lugg on one knee on the rubble, nodding.
line: MERROW: Climbing in, I knocked the lantern on the lip. Eighteen past. Seven wet matches in the dark. Lit again at twenty-five past.
line: MERROW: There. Written by somebody who earned it.
opt: "Write the ferry's turn on the line." -> floor.gap ? has(memory.low_light) & !seen(floor.gap)
opt: "Close the Daybook." -> floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.fight.word.down
place: drowned
cost: 20
do: clear(floor.fight_word); set(merrow.light); quest(a1.lowlight, merrow); set(down.floor); wet(0.8); meter(cold, 2)
nar: The assessor is on the rubble with the sky going round. Merrow sits on the sack, filling a cold pipe.
line: MERROW: You came at Ferris for it. That's earned. Eighteen past I knocked the lantern out. Twenty-five past I had it lit. Between, seven matches and the dark.
opt: "Write the ferry's turn on the line." -> floor.gap ? has(memory.low_light) & !seen(floor.gap)
opt: "Get up." -> floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.fight.word.fled
place: drowned
cost: 1
do: clear(floor.fight_word)
nar: Lugg puts his coat back on. Nobody laughs, which is worse.
line: MERROW: Asleep on my boat, then.
go: floor.merrow.menu

@node floor.fight.salvors.win
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
alt: floor.fight.word.win ? has(floor.fight_word)
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: set(struck.lugg); rep(lowco, -1); give(i.copper_sack); set(floor.copper_taken)
nar: It ends in the water: one salvor sitting in it holding his wrist, the other gone, Lugg on one knee on the rubble, whispering.
nar: The sack is at the assessor's feet, and the tide is climbing the rock.
line: MERROW: You'll carry that to the steps yourself, then. Mind the soft place.
voice: condolence: He has whispered since the night he shouted. You put him on his knee. {dc: 6, when: seen(floor.lugg.why.ok)}
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.fight.salvors.yield
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
alt: floor.fight.word.win ? has(floor.fight_word)
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: set(struck.lugg); rep(lowco, -1); give(i.copper_sack); set(floor.copper_taken)
nar: Lugg puts up one long hand, and the crowbars come down.
line: LUGG: Take it. Take it to the Board, and tell them where you found it, and see does it buy you a dry coat.
nar: They go back over the gully on the rope, one by one, without looking back.
line: MERROW: That's the Company told what the Shelf is. They'll remember.
voice: undertow: A hole, the tide, and a sack of somebody else's winter. You won. {dc: 5}
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.fight.salvors.fled
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
alt: floor.fight.word.fled ? has(floor.fight_word)
place: drowned
cost: 1
do: rep(lowco, -1)
nar: The assessor lets go of the sack and leaves the hole quickly. Lugg hands the sack back to Merrow.
line: MERROW: Gully's that way, if you're going.
go: floor.gully.back

@node floor.fight.salvors.down
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
alt: floor.fight.word.down ? has(floor.fight_word)
place: steps
cost: 30
do: wet(1); damp_wet = 1; meter(cold, 3); meter(dread, 2); rep(lowco, -1); set(down.floor)
nar: The assessor wakes with the water at the chin and Merrow's fist in the coat collar, hauling. He puts the assessor down on the lowest dry step.
line: MERROW: Ferris didn't mean the second one. Ferris never means the second one.
nar: The sack went back over the gully with the Company, and half an hour with it. On the steps above, two bell jars have turned to look.
opt: "Climb to the quay." -> quay.hub +2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Fray: e.conger (optional; leave it its hole)
@node floor.conger
place: drowned
cost: 2
nar: In the water at the bottom of the tower something as thick as a thigh turns over and settles under a ledge, where cut glass catches the light.
nar: A head comes out from under the ledge, with the face of a magistrate who has been woken.
line: MERROW: Conger. She's been in the Old Light longer than me. I leave her be and she leaves me the top half. {when: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow)}
opt: "Leave it its hole." -> floor.conger.leave {verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Go down for the glass under the ledge." -> floor.conger.fight {verb: salvage, noise: 0.3}

@node floor.conger.leave
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: The assessor leaves the conger its hole. The head goes back under the ledge. It is the most courteous exchange the assessor has had in Gullet tonight.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.conger.fight
place: drowned
cost: 1
nar: The assessor goes down into the black water to the thigh, reaching for the ledge.
do: fight(e.conger)

@node floor.fight.conger.win
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: drowned
cost: 3
do: give(s.crown_glass); set(floor.salv.crown); wet(0.4); meter(cold, 1)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.crown_glass)
if: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow) => seenas_lowco = ours
nar: The conger goes back under the stones, all of it at once. Under the ledge: a wedge of the Old Light's lens, frosted on the face the sea could reach.
inst: CANDLEMAS: Crown glass, older than Mother's. That frost is what the sea does to glass it keeps. Anything that comes out of the sea sharp did not come out of the sea. {when: has(prism.numbered)}
inst: CANDLEMAS: Crown glass, older than Mother's. The sea is thorough, but it is not quick. {when: !has(prism.numbered)}
nar: Merrow is in the water beside the assessor with his boathook. {when: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow)}
line: MERROW: You'll not do that twice. She won't let you. {when: clock < 23:40 & has(met.merrow)}
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.fight.conger.yield
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: drowned
cost: 2
do: give(s.crown_glass); set(floor.salv.crown); wet(0.4)
if: has(margin.copper) => give(s.crown_glass)
nar: The conger withdraws into a crack too narrow for anything that size. Under the ledge, a wedge of the Old Light's crown glass.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.fight.conger.fled
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: drowned
cost: 1
do: wet(0.4); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The assessor comes up out of the water a good deal faster than down. The glass stays under the ledge.
go: floor.drowned

@node floor.fight.conger.down
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: steps
cost: 25
do: wet(1); damp_wet = 1; meter(cold, 3); meter(dread, 2); set(down.floor)
nar: The water is at the assessor's chin. Somebody has the assessor under the arms and is walking backward through the gully.
nar: It is Merrow, or Lugg; the assessor is not sure which. The assessor is put down on the lowest dry step with a bruise in the shape of a mouth on the forearm.
voice: dark: Something held you under for a moment, very calmly, and then let go. You will think about the calm. {dc: 5}
opt: "Climb to the quay." -> quay.hub +2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Fray: e.gulls (optional, 23:40 to 23:48, with r.fish)
@node floor.gulls.down
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: At twenty to twelve the gulls come down on the fish all at once, loud and shoving, and look for the eye.
line: DILLY: Get off her. Get off. She's not done.
opt: "Drive them off the fish." -> floor.gulls.fight {verb: throw, noise: 0.6}
opt: "Dilly. Your lanterns. Get the children round her with their lanterns." -> floor.gulls.lanterns ? has(met.dilly) {verb: light, noise: 0.5}
opt: "Leave them. Turn the fish with the gulls on it." -> floor.fish.menu

@node floor.gulls.lanterns
place: fish
cost: 2
do: set(floor.gulls_off); rep(lowco, 1)
nar: Dilly whistles through her fingers. Eleven children run in swinging lanterns, and the gulls lift off, offended.
line: DILLY: Lanterns. They don't like a lantern swung. Everybody on the floor knows that.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.gulls.fight
place: fish
cost: 1
do: fight(e.gulls)

@node floor.fight.gulls.win
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: fish
cost: 2
do: set(floor.gulls_off); seenas_lowco = ours
nar: The gulls go up off the fish and come down on the ribs, in a row, with the united disapproval of a vestry.
line: DILLY: You fought gulls. For her. I'll say so to anyone.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fight.gulls.yield
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: fish
cost: 1
do: set(floor.gulls_off)
nar: The gulls give the fish up sideways, complaining, and settle on the ribs to wait.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fight.gulls.fled
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
if: var.fish == stranded => fish = gulls; quest(a1.fish, gulls)
place: fish
cost: 1
nar: The assessor backs off with both arms over the hat. The gulls do not look up. They find the eye.
line: DILLY: You can't run from gulls. They're gulls.
go: floor.fish.menu

@node floor.fight.gulls.down
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
if: var.fish == stranded => fish = gulls; quest(a1.fish, gulls)
place: fish
cost: 20
do: meter(dread, 1); wet(0.3); set(down.floor)
nar: The assessor goes over in the mud under a weather of wings. Then Dilly's face, upside down, and a lantern. Behind her the gulls have the fish.
line: DILLY: You went down. Gulls did that. I'll not tell anyone. I'll tell everyone.
go: floor.fish.menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Fray: e.eels (optional, inside r.gully)
@node floor.eels.choose
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The gully water moves in loops: eels, a hundred grey ropes pulled by nobody.
voice: salt: Through the middle is short and full of them. By the ribs of the Margery Dole is long, and shallower, and theirs less. {dc: 5}
check: "[HEARSAY] Shout for Lugg to throw you the rope." -> floor.call.lugg / floor.call.lugg.fail ? clock < 23:46 {skill: hearsay, dc: 6, verb: throw, noise: 0.9}
opt: "Go back hand over hand along your line on the ribs." -> floor.eels.line ? has(floor.handline) {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Wade straight through the middle." -> floor.eels.fight {verb: wade, noise: 0.4}
opt: "Keep to the ribs of the wreck, the long way." -> floor.eels.ribs +6 {verb: wade, noise: 0.2}

@node floor.eels.ribs
place: gully
cost: 2
nar: The assessor goes the long way, rib to rib. The eels go past below and do not take the assessor personally.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.call.lugg
place: gully
cost: 2
nar: Out of the fog a loop of rope comes flat across the water, and the long pull begins.
go: floor.run.gully.win

@node floor.call.lugg.fail
place: gully
cost: 1
nar: The wind takes the shout up the floor. Somebody on the steps waves back.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.eels.line
place: gully
cost: 2
nar: The assessor goes hand over hand along the line, rib to rib, the sea pulling at the coat and getting nothing.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.eels.fight
place: gully
cost: 1
do: fight(e.eels)

@node floor.fight.eels.win
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: gully
cost: 2
do: wet(0.2)
nar: The eels let go one by one. A very large one goes past at the knee with a small yellow eye full of opinion.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.fight.eels.yield
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: gully
cost: 2
nar: The eels lose interest. There is a great deal of water and silt, and the assessor is not among the more interesting things in it.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.fight.eels.fled
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
do: wet(1); damp_wet = 1; meter(cold, 2)
place: gully
cost: 7
nar: The assessor backs out and goes round by the ribs after all, with something round one boot that lets go only at the second rib, like a relative at a station.
go: floor.gully.go

@node floor.fight.eels.down
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
place: steps
cost: 7
do: wet(1); damp_wet = 1; meter(cold, 3); meter(dread, 1); set(down.floor)
nar: The assessor goes down with eels round both legs and the water over the hat, and is pulled by the collar through shallow water by somebody who goes into the fog unseen. Short. Wide. A sack.
opt: "Climb to the quay." -> quay.hub +2
